        <p>
        Your responses show stewardship-based leadership thinking across multiple contexts. You focus on developing others and view leadership as a sacred responsibility, not a personal opportunity. You resist taking over tasks to get them done faster, and you celebrate when others grow and receive recognition. 
        </p>
        <p><strong>Your strengths:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>You focus on developing others rather than controlling outcomes</li>
            <li>You take initiative to serve and bless others without needing recognition</li>
            <li>You help others become more capable and confident</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Growth opportunities:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Share your stewardship approach to help others develop similar leadership identity</li>
            <li>Look for chances to mentor others in stewardship thinking and in leading without formal authority</li>
            <li>Continue deepening understanding of stewardship principles in complex situations</li>
        </ul>
            
